1
00:04:52,173 --> 00:04:58,173
No man can walk out of his own story.

2
00:09:44,347 --> 00:09:50,347
Rango is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Gore Verbinski.

3
00:14:36,521 --> 00:14:42,521
When Rango, a lost family pet, accidentally winds up in the gritty, gun-slinging town
of Dirt, the less-than-courageous lizard suddenly finds he stands out.

4
00:19:28,695 --> 00:19:34,695
Welcomed as the last hope the town has been waiting for, new Sheriff
Rango is forced to play his new role to the hilt.

5
00:24:20,869 --> 00:24:26,869
Rango / Lars (voice), played by Johnny Depp.

6
00:29:13,043 --> 00:29:19,043
Beans (voice), played by Isla Fisher.

7
00:34:05,217 --> 00:34:11,217
Mayor (voice), played by Ned Beatty.

8
00:38:57,391 --> 00:39:03,391
Rattlesnake Jake (voice), played by Bill Nighy.

9
00:43:49,565 --> 00:43:55,565
Priscilla (voice), played by Abigail Breslin.

10
00:48:41,739 --> 00:48:47,739
Roadkill (voice), played by Alfred Molina.

11
00:53:33,913 --> 00:53:39,913
Rango is a 2011 American animated Western comedy film directed
by Gore Verbinski and written by John Logan.

12
00:58:26,086 --> 00:58:32,086
The film stars Johnny Depp as Rango, with Isla Fisher, Abigail Breslin, Alfred Molina, Bill
Nighy, Harry Dean Stanton, Ray Winstone and Timothy Olyphant in supporting roles.

13
01:03:18,260 --> 01:03:24,260
In the film, an anthropomorphic pet chameleon ends up in the town of
Dirt, an outpost that is in desperate need of a new sheriff.

14
01:08:10,434 --> 01:08:16,434
The film contains a number of references to various other films, including The Shakiest Gun in the West, A Fistful of Dollars, Chinatown,
The Good, the Bad and the Ugly, Once Upon a Time in the West, Cat Ballou, Raising Arizona and Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas.

15
01:13:02,608 --> 01:13:08,608
Verbinski has also cited El Topo as an influence on the film.

16
01:17:54,782 --> 01:18:00,782
Visual effects and animation for the film were
outsourced to Industrial Light & Magic.

17
01:22:46,956 --> 01:22:52,956
Rango premiered on February 14, 2011, at Westwood, Los Angeles, and was
released in the United States on March 4, by Paramount Pictures.

18
01:27:39,130 --> 01:27:45,130
The film received acclaim from critics and grossed $246
million worldwide against a $135 million budget.

19
01:32:31,304 --> 01:32:37,304
At the 84th Academy Awards, Rango won Best Animated Feature.

20
01:37:23,478 --> 01:37:29,478
Following its critical and commercial success, Rango would
lead to the formation of Paramount Animation.

21
01:42:15,652 --> 01:42:21,652
The film explores themes of hero, gunslinger, sheriff, nevada, mayor.

22
01:47:07,826 --> 01:47:13,826
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
